    "body": "Split out of #8457.\n\n## Problem\n`get_node_shape_meta` in `deepspeed/compile/fx.py` picks between `meta[\"val\"]` and `meta[\"example_value\"]` with `or`. When `meta[\"val\"]` is a tensor, that `or` evaluates the tensor's truthiness. As a result:\n- A tensor with more than one element raises `RuntimeError: Boolean value of Tensor with more than one value is ambiguous`.\n- A zero scalar is treated as missing, so the code falls back to a stale `example_value`.\n\nThis only shows up after `pass_propagate_shapes`, which runs FakeTensorProp and fills in `meta[\"val\"]`. Any AutoSP pass that reads shapes after that step can hit it.\n\n## Fix\nCheck `is not None` explicitly.\n\n## Tests\nAdded `TestNodeShapeMeta` to `tests/unit/v1/compile/test_compile_autosp.py`. It covers:\n- a multi-element tensor\n- a zero scalar\n- falling back to `example_value`\n\nBefore the fix, 2 of these tests fail. After the fix, all 3 pass.\n\nHardware: 8× Intel Arc Pro B70 (XPU), torch 2.14.0.dev+xpu, transformers 5.17. The rest of the AutoSP unit tests pass. `TestAutoSPCompile` is not counted: it fails the same way on master in this environment, in the Dynamo Ulysses baseline.\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
    "closed_at": "2026-10-12T00:36:30Z",
